# Force extension-less URLs to redirect (301) to their canonical .html version.
# Netlify's default "pretty URL" behavior serves page.html at /page with a 200,
# creating duplicate-content URLs. These rules eliminate that by redirecting
# the extension-less path before Netlify's default rewrite can serve it.
# NOTE: Do not add a rule for "/" -> "/index.html" — the homepage should stay at "/".

